## Open Source Community Contribution Terms and Intellectual Integrity Policy

1. GRANT OF CONTRIBUTION LICENSE:
   By submitting a Pull Request, code, assets, or documentation to ArcadeVerse
   (Nexus Spring Of Code - Winter Edition 2026), the contributor certifies that:
   (a) The submission is their original creative work or is licensed under a compatible
       permissive open-source license.
   (b) The contributor grants the ArcadeVerse project, its maintainers, and downstream
       users a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license to use, reproduce,
       distribute, and modify the contribution under the terms of the MIT License.

2. ARCHITECTURAL AND DIRECTORY INTEGRITY:
   All community mini-games must reside strictly inside isolated folders using the
   prescribed notation `games/<game-name_contributor-name>/` to protect project structure
   and prevent merge collisions.

3. ETHICAL CONDUCT AND CODE OF MERIT:
   Contributors agree not to submit malicious scripts, obfuscated payloads, proprietary
   copyrighted third-party assets, or spam commits. Any breach empowers project admins
   to immediately close, revert, and reject offending contributions.
